Registration of Motor Vehicles Repairing Workshop (The Motor Vehicles Rules, 1984 - এর সংশোধনী)
বাংলাদেশ গেজেট (অতিরিক্ত সংখ্যা) > প্রজ্ঞাপন > "70A. Registration of Motor Vehicles Repairing Workshop.—

**কর্তৃপক্ষ কর্তৃক প্রকাশিত**  
**রবিবার, মার্চ ৬, ২০১১**

**গণপ্রজাতন্ত্রী বাংলাদেশ সরকার**  
**যোগাযোগ মন্ত্রণালয়**  
**সড়ক ও রেলপথ বিভাগ**  
**পরিবহন অধিশাখা-২**

**তারিখ:** ১৮ ফাল্গুন ১৪১৭ বঙ্গাব্দ/২ মার্চ ২০১১ খ্রিস্টাব্দ

**এস, আর, ও নং ৪৭-আইন/২০১১।**—The Motor Vehicles Ordinance, 1983 (Ord. No. LV of 1983) এর section 84 এর sub-section (1) এ প্রদত্ত ক্ষমতাবলে সরকার, The Motor Vehicles Rules, 1984 এ নিম্নরূপ অধিকতর সংশোধন করিল, যথা :—

উপরি-উক্ত Rules এর—

(ক) rule 70 এর পর নিম্নরূপ নতুন rule 70A, 70B, 70C, 70D, 70E সন্নিবেশিত হইবে, যথা :—

---

(1) No person or body of persons or establishment shall carry on or engage in the business of repair and maintenance of motor vehicles without registration granted by the registering authority under sub-rule (2) in the Form A.M.W.C.

(2) The registering authority for registration of motor vehicle repairing workshop shall be—

* **(b)** that the persons employed to repair the vehicles have relevant technical knowledge in automobiles;
* **(c)** that the applicant is financially sound;
* **(d)** that the proprietor maintains an adequate space to accommodate at least 5 vehicles of the category for which he has applied for;
* **(e)** that the proprietor has valid trade license, Tax Identification Number (TIN) and other necessary documents;
* **(f)** that the applicant maintains a record of history with vehicle registration number repaired from time to time, name and identification of repaired or replaced parts, the dates etc;
* **(g)** that the applicant maintains suitable tools, equipment and other necessary instruments for repair and maintenance motor vehicles;
* **(h)** that the age of applicant is not below 20 years at the time of application.

(6) The registering authority may refuse to grant registration of a motor vehicle repairing workshop, if the conditions under sub-rule (5) are not fulfilled.

(7) The registering authority may by an order from time to time—
* **(a)** determine procedure for establishment, operation and control of motor vehicle repairing workshop;
* **(b)** determine terms and condition of motor vehicle repairing workshop;
* **(c)** classify motor vehicle repairing workshop for imparting repair and maintenance of light or heavy or other type of motor vehicle;

(8) Any change in the address of the place of business of a motor vehicle repairing workshop shall, within fifteen days of such change, be informed in writing to the registering authority.

(9) Every motor vehicle repairing workshop, its records, equipment, tools and machinery shall be opened at all reasonable times for inspection by the Director (Operation) of Bangladesh Road Transport Authority or any other officer authorized by him in this behalf or the registering authority of that workshop or any other officer authorized by him.

